<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import RouteReadoutDemo from "$ui/demos/pages/routing/RouteReadoutDemo.abide"
  import PageReadDemo from "$ui/demos/pages/data/PageReadDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Data &amp; props</h1>
  <p class="lead">A page and a layout take <strong>no props</strong> — there is no loader convention and no data argument. Everything a page needs comes from two isomorphic sources: <code>route()</code> for the URL and its params, and awaited <strong>reads</strong> for server data. <code>props&lt;T&gt;()</code> belongs to <a href="/templating/components">components</a>, not pages.</p>
  <Demo id="data-route" title="Route data — <code>route()</code>" client="src/ui/demos/pages/routing/RouteReadoutDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <RouteReadoutDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p><code>route()</code> is the same reactive accessor on both sides: <code>route().params</code> holds captured <code>[name]</code> segments, plus <code>.url</code>, <code>.name</code>, <code>.kind</code>, and <code>.navigating</code>. Reading a field re-renders on navigation.</p>
  </aside>
  <Demo id="data-read" title="A read, awaited in the page" server="src/server/rpc/rpcGreet.ts" client="src/ui/demos/pages/data/PageReadDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <PageReadDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>There is no separate loader. To put server data on a page, <code>await</code> a read in the template: it blocks the SSR render so the value lands in the initial HTML, then seeds hydration so the client doesn't re-fetch. Feed <code>route().params</code> straight in when the data depends on the URL.</p>
    <p class="note"><code>props&lt;T&gt;()</code> is a <em>component</em> mechanism. A page or layout is the top of the render — nothing invokes it with props, so its <code>props()</code> is always empty. Reach for <code>route()</code> and reads here; use <code>props()</code> when you factor markup out into a component.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
